subproblem.statement:
Let N ∈ ℕ, M ⊆ ℝᴺ (ℝᴺ = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) = Rn N), φ : ℝ → ℝᴺ → ℝᴺ and y ∈ ℝᴺ. Write:
- X := initialVelocity φ and Z := initialAcceleration φ;
- T_y := tangentSpace M y;
- B_y(τ, η) := secondFundamentalForm M y τ η;
- H(y) := meanCurvature M y.

Assume:
(S) B_y(τ, η) = B_y(η, τ) for all τ, η ∈ T_y;
(N) ⟨η, DX(y)τ⟩ = −⟨X(y), B_y(τ, η)⟩ for all τ, η ∈ T_y;
(H) ⟨X(y), H(y)⟩ = 0.

Then secondVariationIntegrand M φ y = tangentialDivergence M Z y + stableSecondVariationIntegrand M φ y. That is, at y:
div_M Z + (div_M X)² + Σ_i |(D_{τ_i}X)^⊥|² − Σ_{i,j} (τ_i·D_{τ_j}X)(τ_j·D_{τ_i}X) = div_M Z + Σ_i |(D_{τ_i}X)^⊥|² − Σ_{i,j} (X·B(τ_i,τ_j))².

